# Example .gboard for a typical Android project. Copy it to your project root and keep the lines your build has.
# AI agents: use these task names instead of guessing. `gboard print testDebugUnitTest=changed` gives the
# exact command, `gboard list` shows this table.
#
# step  | label                                | gradle task                | where   | auto
#   step   run order: 1 clean, 2 changes files, 3 checks, 4 tests, 5 build, 6 reports (1-2 run as their own build first)
#   where  module = you pick modules, root = whole project (just a tick), :name = always that module
#   auto   "auto" = ★ Auto adds it, on the modules changed on your branch

# Clean
1 | Clean                                | clean                      | root

# Formatting (changes files, so it runs before everything else)
2 | Ktlint: fix formatting               | ktlintFormat               | root
2 | Spotless: fix formatting             | spotlessApply              | root

# Checks
3 | Ktlint: check formatting             | ktlintCheck                | root    | auto
3 | Detekt (static analysis)             | detekt                     | root    | auto
3 | Android lint                         | lintDebug                  | module  | auto

# Tests
4 | Unit tests                           | testDebugUnitTest          | module  | auto
4 | Screenshot tests: verify (Paparazzi) | verifyPaparazziDebug       | module
4 | Screenshot tests: record (Paparazzi) | recordPaparazziDebug       | module
4 | Instrumented tests (needs a device)  | connectedDebugAndroidTest  | module

# Builds
5 | Build debug APK                      | assembleDebug              | :app
5 | Install debug APK on device          | installDebug               | :app
5 | Build release bundle                 | bundleRelease              | :app

# Reports
6 | Coverage report (Kover)              | koverHtmlReport            | root
6 | Dependency updates report            | dependencyUpdates          | root
